# 9. Online and Offline Architecture

## 9.1 Offline-first operation

The application must continue working during internet outages.

Offline features:

- POS billing.
- Cash sales.
- Customer khata.
- Expense entry.
- Inventory updates.
- Product search.
- Customer records.
- Receipt generation.
- Local reports based on synchronized and local data.

## 9.2 Online features

When internet is available:

- Cloud synchronization.
- Online payments.
- Multi-branch updates.
- Cloud backups.
- AI services.
- Payment verification.
- Remote owner dashboard.
- Digital invoices.
- Online ordering.

## 9.3 Synchronization system

Use:

- Local encrypted database.
- Unique transaction IDs.
- Event-based synchronization.
- Retry queue.
- Duplicate transaction prevention.
- Conflict detection.
- Sync status.
- Failed-sync alerts.
- Recovery after application restart.

Financial records must never be silently overwritten using simple last-write-wins synchronization.

The system must maintain transaction history and audit trails.

## 9.4 Important payment limitation

Offline accounting and cash transactions can work without internet.

However, actual online bank, Raast, card, JazzCash or Easypaisa settlement cannot be confirmed without the relevant payment provider's response.

An offline payment request must remain pending until confirmed by the provider. Never display an unverified payment as successfully received.

